{
  "id": 20,
  "name": "return_aware_dual_ramp",
  "intent": "Invert the regret ramp so early picks (where uniform instances need uniqueness ranking because distances collapse) get strong regret weighting (~0.35), decaying to ~0.10 as local distance structure emerges and progress-ramped return bias takes over for late-stage commit. Add a cluster_density-modulated nearest_remaining term (decays with progress) so dense early candidates get bounded lookahead boost without overriding return-aware commitment. Hypothesis: uniform benefits from early regret dominance; clustered/grid are protected because their informative distance ranking makes regret less critical early, and the return ramp still drives final assembly.",
  "tags": [
    "return_aware",
    "regret"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    progress = f[\"progress\"]\n    cluster_density = f[\"cluster_density\"]\n    rw = 0.2 + 0.45 * progress\n    rgw = 0.35 - 0.25 * progress\n    cl = 0.12 * cluster_density * (1.0 - progress)\n    return -f[\"distance\"] + rw * f[\"return_distance\"] + rgw * f[\"regret\"] + cl * f[\"nearest_remaining\"]",
  "source": "live_llm",
